But you have the wherewithal.

There's no spell of Bless. NetHack Is Not D&D. 

Erm, some people might consider this spoilers. Minor spoiler space.

















Blessing is done by dipping objects in holy water. Objects that stack
can be blessed by the stack. And it's recursive: holy water is water
that's been blessed. You know how to make plain water from useless
potions, don't you? Don't forget to either drop and pick up the water
so it stacks or #adjust it all to one slot, or you'll waste holy water
blessing it.

Holy water isn't very wet: it won't do anything to your scrolls and
spellbooks except bless them.

The same goes for cursing and unholy water, of course.

   Raisse, killed by a potion of holy water

